@* A region whose content is still on its way. The blocks inside are decorative, so the announcement is
   made once here instead of a dozen meaningless boxes being read out: a screen reader hears that the
   screen is loading, which is what the spinner it replaces used to say.

   The caption is the shell's own "loading" by default; a region that stands for something more specific
   than the screen - a single block inside an already drawn page - names its own wait instead. *@
<div class="aiko-skeleton-region" role="status" aria-label="@(Label ?? Loc.Get("LoadingContext"))">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The blocks that draw the shape of what is coming.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the wait is called, or null for the screen's own loading caption.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }
}
